520 - He Hideth My Soul
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 520
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[G]A wonderful Savior [Am/C]is Jesus [C/G]my [G7]Lord,
[G7]A wonderful Savior to me,
[G7]He hideth my soul [Am/E]in the cleft of the [C/G]rock,
[G7/D]Where rivers of [Dm]pleasure I see.

Refrain:
[Em]He hideth [G/D]my soul in the cleft [C]of [G7]the rock
[G7]That shadows a dry, thirsty land;
[C/G]he hideth my life in [Am]the depths of His [C]love,
[C]And covers me there with His hand,
[C]And covers me there [Dm]with [G7/F]His hand.

Verse 2:
[G]A wonderful Savior [Am/C]is Jesus [C/G]my [G7]Lord,
[G7]He taketh my burden away,
[G7]He holdeth me up, [Am/E]and I shall not be [C/G]moved,
[G7/D]He giveth me [Dm]strength as my day.

Verse 3:
[G]With numberless blessings [Am/C]each moment [C/G]He [G7]crowns,
[G7]And filled with His fullness divine,
[G7]I sing in my rapture, [Am/C]Oh, Glory to [C/G]God
[G7/D]For such a Redeemer [Dm]as mine.

Verse 4:
[G]When clothed in His brightness, [Am/C]transported [C/G]I [G7]rise
[G7]To meet Him in clouds of the sky,
[G7]His perfect salvation, [Am/C]His wonderful [C/G]love,
[G7/D]I'll shout with the [Dm]millions on high.
